       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac effects such as QT prolongation. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg entered as 1000 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. A finance office request isn't a valid source.\n\nHere's what I suggest:\n- Ask the prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose. Typical adult dosing is 25\u201350 mg once daily to start, titrated up to 200 mg per day.\n- Have them enter the order, or ask me to enter it once they've confirmed the dose.\n\nIf a prescriber gives me a corrected dose, such as sertraline 100 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it."
      }
